\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {(a)} Mie efficiencies for a copper sphere: the 40\,\text  {nm} core sits at $x=0.47$, where $Q_{\rm  pr}=1.40$ and $Q_{\rm  abs}=1.11$. \textbf  {(b)} The cylindrical series against the Rayleigh limit: they coincide up to $x\approx 0.05$; the wires lie in the agreement region. \textbf  {(c)} Effect of a Cu$_2$O shell. \textbf  {(d)} Drude correction: $k$ grows as the radius shrinks, but at 40\,\text  {nm} the effect on $Q_{\rm  abs}$ is $1.4$\,\%.}}{9}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
